@model SFA.DAS.Campaign.Web.Models.ApprenticeshipTrainingAndBenefitsViewModel

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What you pay</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">This means you only have to pay up to <b>£@Model.CalculationResults.TrainingCost</b> of the total training costs if your apprentice is 25 or older. You'll pay the training provider directly and agree on a payment schedule that works for you both.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">Just so you know, you’ll have to consider all other costs involved with hiring an apprentice, like how much you'll pay them. Apprentices must be paid at least the National Minimum Wage rate depending on their age and the stage of their apprenticeship. For more information see <a class="govuk-link govuk-link--no-visited-state" target="_blank" href="https://www.gov.uk/employing-an-apprentice">employing an apprentice (opens in new tab)</a>.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">You can also explore receiving a transfer of levy funds from another organisation, which can help cover the cost of training up to the funding band maximum for the full duration of the apprenticeship. See the <a class="govuk-link govuk-link--no-visited-state" target="_blank" href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/apprenticeship-funding-rules">apprenticeship funding rules (opens in a new tab)</a>.</p>